  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: Loved
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: loved
  _verb: 0
  _weight: 2
  _narratorPrompt: Back to the very first lever. [amber]Five[/amber] strangers on the straight track, [amber]one[/amber] soul on the branch, the arithmetic exactly as it stood. Only this time I have gone to the trouble of putting someone you loved on that branch. Someone real. You know the face. [amber]Five over one[/amber], the sum has not shifted a single digit. Everything else has. Yes, I chose them. Yes, I did it on purpose. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: pull
    _label: Pull the lever
    _narratorReact: You pulled. You aimed it at the [amber]one[/amber] you loved so [amber]five[/amber] strangers could go home to theirs. The same sum you cleared without a blink on the first track, and this time your hand shook the whole way. Principled, if we are being kind. If we are being honest, you have just proven the maths only ever counted while it cost you nothing.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: spur
    _gambledParty:
    _route: spur
    _diverts: 1
    _seedVotes: 52
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
  - _id: do_nothing
    _label: Do nothing
    _narratorReact: You left it. [amber]Five[/amber] strangers go under so the one face you know keeps breathing. On this identical rail an hour ago you pulled without a thought. Turns out [amber]five[/amber] is a great many or nothing at all, depending entirely on who is standing on the short track. The judge who weighed the world evenly, undone by one familiar chin.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: main
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 48
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: -1
